  "compatibility_decisions": [
    "The actual SET_FLAG interpreter uses a word count and searches only the common section. Generated flag states follow that resident ABI, despite the unused SET_FLAG_STR byte declaration.",
    "CP775 character E0 (O with acute) uses a zero output scan to preserve literal character input through both BIOS and DOS CON. Explicit Lithuanian scan remaps remain intact. This follows src/BIOS/MSCON.ASM CHRIN, which classifies E0 with a nonzero scan as a special key.",
    "LITERAL_FF=10h is an opt-in translation-table option. For an FF character and a non-FF scan, KEYB uses its existing BUFFER_FILL_ANY_CHAR entry. All other tables retain the historical character/scan FF ignore sentinels. Latvian AltGr+1 requires literal FF for nonbreaking space.",
    "The expanded library shares the Russian body without changing any bytes. Standalone pre-Baltic library SHA256 f6c776c95ec4b8bda1d72e93233995d76155a2d558283d7ce215def8f23a159e; body SHA256 dba69ef0499cd9dccc96d13d54a933d3e57ce99ee59b6bfc347ef042dcff9255.",
    "The full Russian keyboard suite uses the final expanded library and matching KEYB executable, including physical/DOS input, modifier edges, RU/GR/RU reloads, recipe and rejected-resource/selection cases. Baltic runtime runs select default codes; explicit IDs and EE alias have structural checks only in this stage."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Expanded library selection/reload/rejection matrix for every Baltic code, explicit IDs and EE alias; US/national hotkeys.",
    "Pending dead-key unmatched/repeated/control/reload lifecycle, modifier combinations beyond the direct plane walk and all BIOS fallbacks.",
    "HIGH/LOW memory-profile qualification and supported AT-84/XT-83 real-BIOS input, including the literal-byte extension.",
    "Installed resources/recipes, physical COMMAND/EDLIN and national filename workflows, missing/malformed resources and full BALTIC.md release gates.",
    "Update runtime/mutation artifact coverage for the expanded library and EGA775 pack during packaging."
  ],
  "expected_include_scope": "The retained expected.bin is the final compiled phase for multi-program reload/rejection cases. The full ordered input oracle is retained in each run report.",
